<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 0.54 pct below parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 0.54 pct below parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4735 to the dollar, down from 3.4660 on Friday and at 1.8565 to the mark, up from 1.8720, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.54 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Friday's fix at -0.87 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
